// The Solvent (bible 8.3): a Cantor crew un-anchoring a mill on the Old Road that did not ask. Or did it?
// Ferrow's Mill, Road_3. Sister Wend (dove, Cantor) has the solvent; Miller Tobin did not ask; his mother did.
// The same question Teodor carries about Ettle, from the other side.

title: Road_Solvent
---
<<if has_flag("verdance.solvent.decided")>>
    <<if flag("verdance.solvent.decided") == 1>>
        Tobin: The wheel's still. Mother is glad. I am getting used to it. That is the same thing, some days. #still #line:0fa8a35
    <<elseif flag("verdance.solvent.decided") == 2>>
        Tobin: Still turning. Still the same flour. Mother will not speak to me. The wheel does. #still #line:0a9f6cd
    <<else>>
        Tobin: We are still talking about it. Mother and I. First time in years. The wheel can wait. #still #line:0fd481c
    <<endif>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Wend: Stand clear, Guild. The mill is being let go. The ledger says it asked. #line:0ecff77
Tobin: I never asked! Nobody asked me! The wheel turns. It has turned the same for thirty years. That is fine! #line:0ddec3d
Wend: Your mother asked. She signed for the house. The house is the mill. #line:0e7dcbc
-> Let them do it. #line:0743860
    <<voice drift verdance>>
    Wend: Thank you. It is a small bell. It will not take long. #line:03ffb77
    Tobin: Mother. Mother, what did you do. #line:0348de3
    <<flag verdance.solvent.decided 1>>
-> Stop. He didn't ask. #line:0d3ed7e
    <<voice warden verdance>>
    Wend: Then we are finished here. We do not let go what anyone still holds. Mark that, Guild. #line:059f9e1
    <<flag verdance.solvent.decided 2>>
-> Ask his mother. With him there. #line:0ca0d87
    <<voice surveyor verdance>>
    Wend: That is not how the ledger works. #line:08da8e7
    Tobin: It is how a family works. Mother? Come down. Please. #line:0703d9e
    <<flag verdance.solvent.decided 3>>
===
